From: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] srgn: size the kernel CMA pool from the probed DRAM size

The CMA pool size is a DRAM-size decision, not a board-revision one: the
32M (F1C100s) and 64M (F1C200s) parts share one kernel device tree, and
until now each board dtsi carried its own hardcoded linux,cma size. That
breaks as soon as a revision ships with either die.

Reserved-memory sizing cannot be made self-adjusting on the kernel side
either -- memblock happily satisfies an oversized reservation and starves
the kernel instead of failing. U-Boot already knows the real size from
the DRAM probe, so patch it into the blob in ft_board_setup, after the
overlays have been applied.

The DT keeps the smaller 16M value as its default so that a board still
boots if this fixup never runs.

--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -917,6 +917,42 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Grow the kernel's default CMA pool to 32M on the 64M parts. The node is
+ * located by its linux,cma-default property rather than by path so that
+ * adding further reserved regions later does not silently pick the wrong one.
+ */
+static void srgn_fixup_cma_size(void *blob)
+{
+	int rmem, node;
+	u32 size;
+
+	rmem = fdt_path_offset(blob, "/reserved-memory");
+	if (rmem < 0)
+		return;
+
+	size = (gd->ram_size > 32 * 1024 * 1024) ? (32 << 20) : (16 << 20);
+
+	fdt_for_each_subnode(node, blob, rmem) {
+		int ret;
+
+		if (!fdt_getprop(blob, node, "linux,cma-default", NULL))
+			continue;
+
+		ret = fdt_setprop_u32(blob, node, "size", size);
+		if (ret)
+			printf("srgn: CMA fixup failed: %s\n",
+			       fdt_strerror(ret));
+		else
+			printf("srgn: CMA %u MiB (DRAM %lu MiB)\n",
+			       size >> 20,
+			       (unsigned long)(gd->ram_size >> 20));
+		return;
+	}
+
+	printf("srgn: no linux,cma-default node, CMA fixup skipped\n");
+}
+
 int ft_board_setup(void *blob, bd_t *bd)
 {
 	int __maybe_unused r;
@@ -927,6 +963,8 @@
 	 */
 	setup_environment(blob);
 
+	srgn_fixup_cma_size(blob);
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_VIDEO_DT_SIMPLEFB
 	r = sunxi_simplefb_setup(blob);
 	if (r)
